/** kereti, peleti, pitchei-teshuva, nekudot, kaf-hachayim, mateh-yehonatan, yad-avraham, yad-ephraim, rabbi-akiva-eiger-yd */
export default {
  kereti: {
    '1#א': `Kivah is the meses — from the meses food enters the kivah; and this does not exist in fowl at all.`,
    '1#ב': `Chelev on the yeter — see below siman 64 where everything is explained.`,
    '2#א': `Kereis punctured — and the spleen does not seal, because the spleen membrane interrupts and tame chelev.`,
    '2#ב': `Treifah — they slaughtered the animal or fowl and much water and intestinal fluid flowed — all is fine and kosher; it is weakness common in man called Wassersucht from swelling; one should not multiply treifah declarations; and so from Bach's responsum.`,
    '2#ג': `And you have nothing that seals — see Peleti where I discussed well whether chelev that Ashkenazim eat seals in communities that practice among many even to forbid it — and it is full chelev; and see settling Maharshal's difficulty and Kuntres on Peri Chadash and Sha'ar Efrayim.`,
    '2#ד': `Kosher; and if the kereis was punctured — whether to suspend that after slaughter the many opinions spread to permit, among them Peri Chadash — beautiful ruling; see below siman 50 in Peleti.`,
    '3#א': `If it tears — all this is through illness; but if through knife and the like and it reached the cavity of the body — treifah like a needle in the cavity of the body — Taz; and simple.`,
    '3#ב': `Most thickness of the flesh — this is Rambam's view; most authors disagree and we require specifically mafpolash. And see Peleti where I wrote Rambam has proof from the Gemara — see there; and I left a difficulty on Tosafot — therefore where there is no great loss, treifah according to Rambam.`,
    '3#ג': `And how much measure — this measure applies even in mafpolash — we also require this measure.`,
    '3#ד': `Most of the length — the same applies to most of the width; and the poskim mentioned one of them.`,
    '4#א': `Or in length — meaning there is deficiency; if you make a circle from it — it is like a sela; but in the previous seif it deals only with tear without deficiency — if so, even if a circle from it would not be a third of a tefach, nevertheless since its length is a tefach — treifah — Shach.`,
    '4#ב': `If it was more. See Peleti: punctures with deficiency join to a sela; punctures without deficiency join to a majority; and see what I analyzed there.`,
    '4#ג': `It will stand at a tefach — and if it is small and does not hold a tefach but only two-thirds of a tefach — ostensibly if bored like half a sela it is also treifah, for if stretched it will be a third and a half which is the majority of two-thirds of a tefach; and see Peleti — requires further study; it appears the view leans to permit — see there.`,
    '7#א': `Even, etc. — and korat dam is not required from outside for Rashi; but from inside — Shach's view requires korat dam, otherwise after slaughter it was stuck; and see Peleti where I brought supports from the Gemara — since in any case most authors disagree with Rashi, one may be lenient without korat dam from inside; and see Peleti where I challenged Rashi — and I wrote Rashi may concede regarding a needle that korat dam is required.`,
    '7#ב': `And so is the practice — Shach and Taz's view is specifically through a needle; but not through illness; even for that view which is Rashi's view we are not concerned; and see Peleti where I challenged on this; therefore in a place of loss even through illness one should be stringent.`,
    '7#ג': `If not, etc. — and if it swallowed before us and they slaughtered immediately and it is found stuck from one side in the meses — Tosafot's view at end of "With what may we light" — in this even Rashi permits; and see Peleti where I brought supports from Tosafot in Chullin — and one may rely on them.`,
    '8#א': `And korat dam found on it — specifically on it opposite the puncture from inside — so agreed most poskim; and if korat dam alone is found without puncture from inside, even if needle lies in beit hakosot — kosher — so agreed acharonim, not like Shach.`,
    '8#ב': `Kosher — and korat dam from inside does not cause treifah; and Shach reconciles that we are concerned in esophagus lest it healed — and see what I wrote siman 33 — for us there is no difference — see in Peleti.`,
    '8#ג': `A bit of outer skin — even for Rashi who forbids in the meses.`,
    '8#ד': `And this is when they did not salt. See Peleti where I brought that initially examination is certainly required after korat dam — only here it deals when not examined and salted — thereby the apparent contradiction in Tur is resolved.`,
    '8#ה': `Or it was lost — and if not examined at all to see if punctured outward — Peri Chadash's view is to be stringent; and he is correct.`,
    '8#ו': `And one may rely — and see Peleti where I proved from Tosafot that examination is always required — therefore one should be stringent.`,
    '8#ז': `Around the needle — in this even from the side of the puncture — treifah — so wrote the poskim.`,
    '8#ח': `And one may rely — and Taz is stringent; and so there are luminaries.`,
    '9#_': `Rust — meaning on the head of the needle where we doubt whether the point passed outward before or after slaughter; we say rust testifies it passed before slaughter; but in the middle of the needle rust makes no difference, for certainly it punctured and came from life; rust only perhaps did not pass the entire thickness until mafpolash — and simple; and so Maharshal.`,
    '11#א': `And if there is no korat dam on it — in this it appears certainly obligatory to examine after korat dam; for otherwise some are stringent to say it came from outside — and then for everyone examination is required.`,
    '11#ב': `And some are stringent unless there is recognition it came from inside — and see Peleti where I brought proof that Tosafot also permit — therefore one may lean lenient.`,
  },
  peleti: {
    '1#_': `And if the chelev, etc. — see what I wrote at length in siman 64 — see there.`,
    '2#א': `Kereis, etc., and you have nothing to seal it — Taz wrote s.k. 2: that the spleen does not seal because of the spleen membrane that interrupts; and I did not understand — the chelev covering the kereis interrupts between the kereis and spleen and it is tame chelev — how does the spleen seal.`,
    '2#ב': `That it seals it — certainly for those who hold like Rabbenu Yoel; if so it is obvious fat adhering to the kereis that they eat certainly seals; and Rambam holds like Rabbenu Efrayim that it is tame chelev; and that Rama did not emend for us that fat seals — since the people of Rhineland eat it; if so they eat forbidden food, etc. — see what I wrote on this siman 64; I did not understand him; nor that Rashi wrote tame chelev does not seal because it is not attached but a resident; and Rashba in Tur haArukh 37 wrote tame chelev does not seal because there is a membrane below; and he explains "they eat" chelev of yeter — they eat forbidden chelev of yeter because it is not attached, meaning the membrane does not interrupt between it and the flesh, etc. — and from this reason the law is that it should seal even for Babylonians; and if so this fat adhering that R' Eliezer and R' Yoel fought about is the fat adhering to the kereis itself and the membrane is above it — if so what difference whether forbidden or permitted — in the end it is not attached and seals. And one may say Rambam deduced from "they eat," etc. — and for us sealing does not seal as explained. And with this Maharshal's wonder in Orach Chaim siman 54 on R' Yehudah Zahav who doubted in that siman whether it seals — and he is included in "they eat," etc. — is settled; and he wondered why according to R' Eliezer it is karet prohibition — it is only a stringency of the law like R' Akiva who requires attachment; but all agree it is not attached and certainly seals. And why wonder on "they eat" — since all Israel do not eat the kivah it would not seal even though not attached; whereas since the people of Eretz Yisrael eat it, the reason "they do not divide" does not apply; and since it is not attached — it seals. Therefore the kereis — since Rambam holds like R' Eliezer and it is forbidden as chelev and karet punishment — therefore "they eat" does not apply; unlike chelev on the yeter which is only a general stringency — we properly say "they eat," etc. And with this Peleti settles Sha'ar Efrayim and Peri Chadash who debated wisely on a needle at the head of the dekin that chelev seals the puncture whether to permit because many poskim hold "head of intestine" refers only to the end of the intestines near the stomach and it is in the category of "they eat" — see there; and why did they trouble with this — it is explained in Mordechai that "head of intestine" is not attached at all — if so obviously it seals; and what difference tame or pure — and according to my words it is fine that even if we say even though not attached it does not seal — examine well.`,
    '3#_': `Even though this tear did not reach the kereis, etc. — Rambam's view; most authors disagree as the acharonim wrote. To me: perhaps this membrane that Rashi said covers the paunch in its majority is attached to that membrane as known — if so when the thick membrane is torn, the chelev covering the kereis is attached to it — difficulty for R' Shimon who holds tame chelev seals. If so how can chelev seal the puncture — therefore Rambam holds we do not require mafpolash puncture; and sealing does not help him as above siman 46 — see Taz. Or one may say in the Gemara 52b in Samuel's matter "flesh covering most of the kereis in its majority" — Rav Ashi asked whether R' Eliezer means torn in its majority or majority removed; difficulty: open the first chapter — we establish all 18 treifot as eight punctures counted as one category entering and exiting — the Gemara asks if so punctures too, etc., but those two categories should not exit — the kereis is missing "removed" also in the mishnah; and if stolen from it impossible not to find a single one in the book; and it is not that Rashi's view is not in any way that Samuel holds like the majority — if the majority is torn from it it is revealed more than removal; and if removed from it impossible to find single — and why did he write this law unlike the spleen specifically here; one may say because he gave a general rule in siman 50, etc. — not helpful here to give measure but removal in circle or length with deficiency like sela; Tur wrote "or removed in it" — scribal error for "all of it"; Shulchan Aruch does not reconcile — he wrote first or removed meaning bored; seif 4 already wrote its law. Or our membrane is thin attached to paunch membrane — R' Shimon seals; Rambam not; sealing not helpful; see Taz. Or Gemara 52b Samuel — majority torn or majority removed; difficulty 18 treifot; missing removed in mishnah; Rashi majority torn; removal impossible find single; why unlike spleen; siman 50 rule; measure for bored; Tur error; Shulchan Aruch Rambam bored; seif 4. Or thin membrane on paunch — R' Shimon; Rambam; Taz. Gemara Rav Ashi; 18 treifot; removed; Rashi; Tur; Shulchan Aruch; thin membrane; Taz. Majority R' Yehudah amoraim; small animal majority length without tefach treifah; Bach wondered Beit Yosef proved Rambam Tur; not nothing; Samuel majority; Rif majority; Rambam Tur tefach large animal; Bach forced; majority width; Rashi necessary fowl; Rif one place; Shulchan Aruch correct Rambam; Taz correct; Peleti forced; Rosh Behag; finger below; Rosh explained; Gemara difficulty return mixed; not Rashi fowl; Rif one root finger; Shulchan Aruch stringent fowl; Rashi first necessary; Taz correct.`,
    '4#_': `If the flesh was bored, etc. — regarding gullet lacking deficiency, cracks join majority; with deficiency join sela; certainly here likewise; we do not say in treifot the derivation from gullet to skull; if cracks together majority or tefach — treifah — simple. According to Shach and Taz siman 33 drawing board long strips — why need specifically sela; even small width can cut long strips without width only length more than tefach — all difficulties on prohibition here in sela; their jeopardy there; my answer above does not sit here; truth analogy if tear like that and beside another — even in length ten tefachim — in truth "join" means lengthwise together; not beside — no difference one or two tears — not stretched more; not take beside to put in length — clear in reason. If bored like sela all lines like that each line not join more length all one stretch — truly should not join only halacha leMoshe miSinai if bored like sela and surround is tefach even not worthy to join nevertheless treifah Torah decree. Settles why "bored like sela" specifically; small animal holds tefach only two-thirds; bored half sela should be treifah stretch third and half majority two-thirds — not in Gemara; measure only sela not half; why; whole measure is kabbalah and halacha leMoshe miSinai; only tefach and majority not half sela — not treifah; examine well.`,
    '7#א': `And thus when it swallowed before us and slaughtered immediately and found stuck as Tosafot second chapter Shabbat imply — even Rashi concedes not concerned lest healed; Tosafot in Chullin in Rashi's words wrote in beit hakosot one side kosher from inside; outside needle in body cavity treifah — must understand relevance to Rashi — in beit hakosot they did not disagree; accordingly wonder even for Rashi why mishnah does not teach meses; if there no need mafpolash as above; if not about that beraisa deals stuck before us — therefore wrote not about stuck uncommon only inside; examine well.`,
    '7#ב': `Even without puncture Shach s.k. 14 wrote simply even korat dam outside not required — simple. Therefore wonder Rashi's forcing in meses not require outward because teaches needle in beit hakosot not meses; also end Shabbat chapter name changed from huvlila to beit kisei — difference needle in beit hakosot forced Rashi explain so; Tosafot difficulty mishnah meses beit hakosot punctured outward; Rabbenu Tam meses too mafpolash; Rashi outward not entirely; R' Yitzchak meses one side; esophagus; mishnah when know not healed ate needle before us; Rabbenu Tam meses mafpolash; Tur poskim Rabbenu Tam Shulchan Aruch; Rama forbid Rashi Terumat HaDeshen Orach Chaim agree; great loss lenient. Now Shach s.k. 14 not require outside; wonder Rashi forcing meses teaches beit hakosot not meses; Shabbat name change; Tosafot mishnah; Rashi; R' Yitzchak; esophagus; Rabbenu Tam; Tur; Rama; Shach. Beraisa needle beit hakosot not meses; Rashi not stuck only inside; Peleti reverse natural needle korat dam even Rashi meses require korat dam; Gemara teaches beit hakosot not meses; Tosafot difficulty; Rashi thin; Ran; Tosafot; Rashi healed; Ra'ash; Tosafot lung; no examination Ra'ash Tur hints esophagus more here; lung only blowing Ra'ash Tur 36 Beit Yosef distinguish there not blown concern puncture not recognizable; here estimation not outward no turn examine; lung thin membranes Maharam distinguish; several manners; Rambam one side kosher no examination Kessef Mishneh needle outside inside no foods liquids all agree kosher; examine.`,
    '7#ג': `Shach wrote s.k. 14 for Rashi forbid meses even without outward clearly treifah even without korat dam outside; inside Shach requires korat dam otherwise after slaughter stuck; sought Tur Choshen Mishpat not found; distinguish inside foods liquids pressed; stuck well after slaughter movement needle inside; Rashba esophagus foods liquids stream not beit hakosot rest; Shach concern after slaughter stuck; greater must say Gemara 49 why not test kofa bar or inside; Rashi kofa stuck wall mouth inside kereis certainly outside; foods liquids pressed kofa enters flesh; still hard beit hakosot kofa toward animal point toward cavity two sides why korat dam; no foods liquids pressed; you say kofa punctured before slaughter by pressure; if after slaughter all quiet no pressure; how say after slaughter; how kofa punctured came after slaughter; still question should distinguish kofa bar inside; ostensibly after slaughter by shaking animal etc. needle stuck even dead animal; Shach law correct by shaking stuck after slaughter; still initially stringent.`,
    '7#ד': `Practice Shach Taz both answer specifically needle concern healed not illness; Lechem already preceded showed all sides; to me why specifically needle; reason lest healed — all Rashi foundation teaches needle beit hakosot not meses; Ulla and supporters not concerned healed; beraisa needle beit hakosot how established meses not concerned healed; if say Ulla concedes thin frequent concern; Ra'ash challenged Rif from beit hakosot to esophagus esophagus soft unlike beit hakosot hard; forced if so why Ulla; if illness too concern healed no need soft esophagus; if illness concern healed both; punctured one without other how find; examine; therefore illness without great loss stringent.`,
    '8#א': `Kosher — see Shach s.k. 19 distinguish esophagus concern healed; wrote above siman 33 not comparable esophagus safek shechitah; more Rambam — see there.`,
    '8#ב': `Around — all agreed from one side require korat dam opposite needle; two sides not required opposite; proves korat dam alone without puncture opposite kosher; otherwise puncture from here korat dam alone would treifah; rather learn korat dam alone not treifah; so Tzitz Eliezer; correct not Shach.`,
    '8#ג': `And some lenient Taz s.k. 12 Shach s.k. 32 elaborated against each other; Taz words not obligatory; Shach difficulty Tur wrote turn over implies obligatory; above thorn esophagus Ra'avan Ra'ash proved Ulla no examination beit hakosot learn no examination; ostensibly needs answer; appears if stuck into skin how not examine — most lungs kosher; minority common need examination; here common since puncture through and only slight remnant also punctured; Tosafot compare safek derusah wrote safek derusah common since common cannot require examination all lungs need examination; here ideally certainly need only if lost without examination lung permitted also here if lost judge need examination b'dieved treifah or only stringency like lost lung kosher same here; Tur turn over wrote ideally examination like lung; above deals if inhibits when lost without examination esophagus no examination inhibits only disqualify lost lung clear; Tosafot somewhat all places need examination; else forced Tosafot Shabbat name change; not resolve simple beit hakosot second skin punctured one no examination two meses one skin need examination difference needle; always examination therefore stringent Taz Bach unless great loss; further arguments settle; if stuck body cavity beit hakosot outside inside not side to side perhaps no examination after korat dam; reverse foods liquids pressed probably common puncture whole need examination; reverse foods liquids block needle not exit outside no concern; simple in reason; no proof Rambam one side kosher no examination Rambam explains needle outside inside no foods liquids all permit; examine.`,
    '11#_': `And some stringent, etc. — Tosafot imply like Rashba lenient Chullin 48b s.v. if kofa, etc. — concluded also if found inside kurkavan kosher because esophagus way needle with food kurkavan hangs on esophagus. If intent plainly needle in kurkavan — obvious all enters body; if treifah kurkavan also beit hakosot in animal treifah — not taught one side kosher what Tosafot here; rather clear: found in thickness of kurkavan swallowed in flesh — do not know inside through esophagus or outside esophagus punctured came; Tosafot like lung taught all from esophagus; kurkavan depends esophagus; inside because near esophagus; wrote kurkavan not beit hakosot — hard reality stuck without mark inside outside; since Tosafot agree to leniency — worthy to rely on them.`,
  },
  'pitchei-teshuva': {
    '1#_': `On the yeter. [See Be'er Heitev; and what he wrote in name of Shulchan Aruch siman 62 that wart is proof it punctured, etc. — see in Sefer Levushei Serad ot 62 and 63 who wrote if found outside a hard place in touch like a nut — requires further study, for perhaps comparable to wart; and plausible this is according to the examiner's eyes in its hardness and nature; and from Peri Megadim siman 49 s.k. 2 one may hear he holds hard flesh is not a defect — see there further; and see what I wrote s.k. 6 in name of Shevut Yaakov:]`,
    '2#_': `Kereis punctured treifah. [See in Sefer Binat Adam gate of prohibition and permission siman 26 who wrote a sharp question: they stabbed between the ribs near the belly and secretion emerged and it appeared the kereis was punctured; and afterward it lived twelve months and also became pregnant and gave birth — what is its law. He answered: ostensibly since secretion emerged, certainly the kereis was punctured — certainly treifah; and it would not help even if it lives many days as siman 57. But after examination it appears this is only safek treifah — for Tur brought view of some that inner kereis is specifically the lower part facing the ground, but above in the rib area if the kereis was punctured it is not treifah except in its majority or a tefach — and this is Ittur's view; but majority of poskim hold kereis punctured anywhere is treifah in any amount; and the annotator in Tur wrote sense and experience testify to the first view — therefore safek dispute; and since it lived twelve months or gave birth — it is kosher, end of his words — see there. In my humble opinion this permit requires further study — since majority of poskim forbid anywhere in any amount as he himself wrote — for Peri Megadim wrote siman 81 s.k. 165 safek dispute where many hold thus — even if alive twelve months one may not permit — see there. And what he brought from Tur annotator, etc. — intent seems even though majority forbid, annotator's words from sense and experience give at least balanced safek. Wonder he did not mention Bach who cried out on that annotation and wrote printers may Heaven save them insert annotation not halacha — see there. However in my humble opinion when the rabbi wished to prove kereis punctured between ribs is only safek treifah — he need not mention Ittur or annotator — seems majority who forbid anywhere in any amount do not concede obviously they hold halacha like Rabbah in chapter Elu Treifot 56b — rather from safek because halacha is doubtful like whom — see Rashi there who wrote since halacha not decided we act stringently and declare treifah entire kereis punctured in any amount; also Ra'ash there siman 33 wrote some hold halacha like Rabbah bar Rav Huna and some like Rabbach; Rashi ruled stringently like R' Yosei bar Chanina and so custom — end of his words. Presumably Tur and other poskim likewise rule stringently since safek d'oraisa — if so only safek treifah and living twelve months or birth helps per assumption safek dispute helps twelve months to permit. However on that main assumption Shach also siman 57 s.k. 48 implies so from Maharshal chapter Elu Treifot siman 80 and his words are correct; and Peri Chadash agreed s.k. 50; and so Peri Megadim and Levushei Serad and responsum Zichron Yosef Yoreh De'ah part 2 siman 2 and several acharonim — nevertheless matters require further study as Sefer Emek Halachah siman 8 wondered: if so what helps living twelve months for safek din — judged from rule whatever safek treifah such as this is kosher; and if we say no proof from living since minority live — how permit this animal; they will say two animals with defect one forbidden one permitted, etc. He concludes there for practical law not like Maharshal who holds twelve months helps safek in the act itself; not so safek in the din, etc. — end of his words; and so I found in Sefer Amudei Or newly printed siman 49 wondered on the sage in the goat incident likewise per that reasoning — if so that goat permitted us kereis puncture between ribs — why distinguish that goat or other animals since from that event the din was decided, etc. — see there. (In truth this wonder is not on the sage but on Maharshal Shach and acharonim who followed him.) Also from Bach's challenge on Tur annotator it is clear he does not hold Maharshal's view — requires further study; and see Turei Beit Shmuel siman 30 s.k. 8 and Sefer Beit Efrayim siman 35 s.k. 100:] (b) For the chelev. Be'er Heitev. And what he wrote regarding swollen chicken — see on this responsum Noda BiYehudah Tinyana Yoreh De'ah siman 25; and I brought it above siman 45. And what he wrote in name of Shevut Yaakov he heard from doctors, etc. — see there he wrote further and similarly I heard regarding chickens whose legs are swollen even the lower bone — concern comes from illness padagra common in chickens and eaters come to this illness — therefore guard your soul distance from them — end of his words:`,
    '3#_': `This tear to the kereis. See in Tiferet Moshe who wrote from this language it implies specifically torn from outside the skin and most of its thickness — not as punctured from inside most thickness while minority remains outside; and so Bach explicitly — see there; and so I ruled practically — end of his words:`,
    '4#_': `Length of the flesh. Be'er Heitev; and see in Tiferet Moshe who wrote the same in diagonal or half circle and the tear is majority or tefach without deficiency — requires further study for practical law — end of his words:`,
    '5#_': `This flesh bored in a circle. See in Tiferet Moshe who wrote in boring a small animal we estimate a third of its majority length or width as in a large animal we estimate third of tefach in boring — requires further study — see there. [And so in Sefer Pithei Teshuvah ot 10; but not view of Turei Beit Shmuel and Kereti and Peleti s.k. 5 — see there; and see Levushei Serad ot 61 who wrote from Taz siman 34 s.k. 3 appears like Pithei Teshuvah that also for majority we say reasoning if stretched; but from Tosafot Orach Chaim 4 it may be proved like Turei Beit Shmuel and poskim that wherever measure is in majority we do not apply "if stretched"; and concludes without great loss one should be stringent like Pithei Teshuvah; but with great loss one may be lenient — see there:]`,
    '6#_': `And so is the practice. [Be'er Heitev; and what he wrote however it appears we require korat dam from inside — see Turei Beit Shmuel who was stringent even without korat dam; and Peri Megadim agreed with Shach — see in responsum Chatam Sofer siman 48 what he wrote on this:]`,
    '7#_': `On it korat dam. Be'er Heitev; what he wrote but if found, etc.; and see in Sefer Nachalat Azriel Chullin daf 51 who wrote Shach comes to explain Beit Yosef's words; but according to what he wrote s.k. 31 even without stuck at all treifah if korat dam outside as Be'er Heitev s.k. 22 — all the more stuck one should forbid even not directly on it; and he wrote further one may say more stringent if not stuck at all — see there:]`,
    '8#_': `Korat dam. Be'er Heitev s.k. 3 in name of Tzitz Eliezer the same for adhesion; and so in responsum Sha'ar Efrayim siman 62 and responsum Chut haShani siman 69 and other acharonim; and see in responsum Shevut Yaakov part 2 siman 64 who wrote adhesion literally in the eye we require; but if slightly swollen outside and somewhat thick and no change in flesh to defect — no treifah, for this comes from pain of needle stuck in live flesh; do not add to treifot — see there. [And see responsum Chatam Sofer siman 42 who wrote what was produced: if recognizable punctured through illness and korat dam outside — do we also say if no wound whence korat dam; this is simpler than "expression in the vessel" — thus: needle thus puncture in general; whatever korat dam opposite it teaches blow ruled there too; slight proof from above siman 40 seif 6; and so from Taz siman 37 end s.k. 3, etc.; but it appears specifically for needle we must turn initially and examine if korat dam outside — for regarding needle it is common that it healed unlike through illness recognizable did not control more. Nay: if korat dam found opposite — treifah; but examination not required for this; and this law is true — end of his words — see there:]`,
    '9#_': `And some lenient to permit. See in Degel Machaneh Efrayim who wrote to decide: where blood was inside — then certainly from life; and did not examine outside for korat dam — then treifah; but if did not examine inside or outside for korat dam and also not punctured from both sides — we say shechutah hutrah; and all the more if saw inside no korat dam and before examining outside it was lost — kosher even not in great loss. And see there it is implied from his words that even according to Shach below siman 57 s.k. 3 who ruled where no great loss even in safek that did not leave presumption from life one forbids — nevertheless here kosher even not in great loss, for there is double safek perhaps after slaughter perhaps not punctured outward — see there:`,
    '10#_': `Forced through and kosher. Sefer HaTe'udah wrote in name of Yam Shel Shlomo: if there is like a recognizable path until outside — treifah, for it appears from life it passed; and he wrote further in name of Tur Choshen Mishpat: specifically when punctures not found immediately when removed from animal but after a day or half day — we may suspect done by man; but if immediately when removed found thus — one may not permit, for certainly done before slaughter. And he wrote on this: for us there is no difference since Rama testified we practice to declare treifah in every manner without korat dam and without rust; nevertheless I wrote for other places that do not practice like Rama, etc. — see there; and see in She'elot uTeshuvot Tolodot Yitzchak siman 5 who wrote on this: even for us there is a difference per Shach s.k. 30 in name of Bach that even punctured from both sides if no korat dam found one may permit in our time in great loss; and so one should rule; nevertheless if there is like a path outside or if immediately when removed found thus — one may not permit even in great loss — see there; and it is simple; and it appears Turei Beit Shmuel for his view who wrote in Orach Chaim 17 one forbids even in great loss punctured from both sides — unlike Shach and Peri Megadim s.k. 30 — properly there is a difference:`,
    '11#_': `No examination. Be'er Heitev; and see what I wrote above s.k. 5 and above siman 41 s.k. 11 on this matter:`,
    '12#_': `Great loss. Be'er Heitev; and what he wrote in name of Taz there is no permit from one side, etc. — see Shevut Yaakov part 2 siman 64 who disagrees with Taz in what he declares treifah if stuck along length even if recognizable from inside — this is not so; Hagahot Shaarei Dura deals only when stuck in it and not recognizable inside or outside whence it came; and in this too one should not be stringent except not in great loss as Shulchan Aruch ruled in kurkavan — see there; and see Peri Chadash who also wrote per Taz it is not essential for practical law; however if stuck from outside along wall of beit hakosot — one should declare treifah — see there. Meaning: in that half-thickness of the wall from the outside side it was stuck inside the flesh along the wall and all swallowed in flesh thickness and no puncture recognizable inside or outside — treifah. Turei Beit Shmuel's view is to be more stringent: even if not stuck but lying along — treifah. Peri Megadim ruled lying — lenient; stuck — even from inside side — treifah. And see in responsum Tolodot Yitzchak siman 4 who elaborated bringing proof for Peri Chadash's view and leaned to permit in great loss; however if also found beit hakosot adhered to liver — then certainly in such a case one may not be lenient even in great loss — see there (see what I wrote above siman 41 s.k. 12 in his name); and see Noda BiYehudah Tinyana Yoreh De'ah end siman 2 who wrote on matter of needle stuck in beit hakosot and length of needle along beit hakosot — if truly stuck along length one may not be lenient except in great loss one may settle — see there:`,
  },
  'nekudot-hakesef': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 48 in Taz s.k. 5) He wrote on Beit Yosef that his words are very astonishing and he elaborated and did not get to the end of his mind — for even though Beit Yosef's language is ambiguous, nevertheless it is simple his intent is specifically tear by knife is in any amount; but not by illness — only he was precise that it deals with not mafpolash since it also deals with knife; and so explicitly in Kesef Mishneh; one examining Kesef Mishneh will see deficiency in Beit Yosef's language; and intent of his words as in Darkei Moshe — see there.`,
    '2#_': `(There s.k. 6) His words are not clear — examine well.`,
    '3#_': `(Taz s.k. 12) His words are astonishing — for Beit Yosef explains Rabbi turned it over by chance; if so Abaye spoke well that he troubled for nothing since this young scholar did not come to teach we must turn it over; also what he wrote regarding Rambam's view is not clear — for Rambam never mentioned law of one side; also what he wrote regarding Ra'ash is certainly not so as Shach s.k. 32 wrote; also what he brought from Rashba's responsum siman 360 — one may say it deals with puncture from two sides; but from one side one may say he holds no examination is required even ideally; and so Maharshal Orach Chaim siman 91 and responsum Ben Lev kelal 9 responsum 3 and Beit Chadash and other acharonim like Rabbi Rama; and so we rule.`,
    '4#_': `(There s.k. 13) And in my humble opinion, etc. — Maharoch and Bach already preceded him in this as Shach s.k. 26 wrote.`,
    '5#_': `(There Taz 17) He copied Darkei Moshe's words and wondered on Beit Chadash; it was hidden from him all Shach wrote siman 49 s.k. 4 that Beit Chadash's words are clear and Darkei Moshe's astonishing; see there. Also what he wrote practice every day declare treifah punctured from both sides even without korat dam outside — no proof from practice, for even in beit hakosot practice is thus because we are not expert in korat dam; and further what they declare treifah is when there is rust which is like korat dam.`,
    '6#_': `(There end s.k. 18) His words are not compelling.`,
    '7#_': `(There s.k. 19) He challenged Maharam for not according to law — for Maharam himself concludes end of that responsum: one may not rely on a gentile since it was stuck in a manner that was not punctured outward, for we do not rely on gentile words neither to forbid nor to permit; and you would say if so we need not believe the gentile that he found the needle stuck, etc. — this is not so, etc., until: if so in our case too — since an Israelite came while the gentile was still dealing with removing the innards from the kereis and found the nail in the gentile's hand with legs to speak — gentile's words are only like revealing a matter in the world; but if after the gentile stopped dealing with removing innards and already removed the kereis from his hand and came to the Jew with this iron nail in hand and said he found it stuck in the kereis — we need not believe him and I have no power to forbid — end of his words. If so all he brought to contradict Maharam is irrelevant here — only general revelation. However requires further study why Maharam concludes there "and I have no power to forbid" except if the Jew was silent — this depends on disputes whether one witness is believed in prohibitions — not to elaborate now. And what is one witness believed in prohibitions regarding a gentile — even for a robber we rule even silent not believed as I wrote siman 127 Shach s.k. 9; all the more a gentile; and it must be Maharam does not refer to the gentile but generally; and because of his method he mentioned the gentile. He further challenged Maharam regarding water in brain not according to law — for Maharam himself wrote there the reason we practice to declare treifah in brain is because it is common; and not as Darkei Moshe's reason the defect was from life; and he did not mention common reason at all; and this is the main reason; and so in hagahah siman 50 he did not mention common reason; and what requires examination is no proof it is common for prohibition; and also what the rabbi wrote there in hagahah even though it is treifah that has examinations — implies all the more treifah without examination — law is thus; and see Shach siman 50 chapter 6 at length on this.`,
  },
  'kaf-hachayim': {
    '1#_': `(1) [Seif 1] Kivah punctured — treifah; and if chelev on the yeter seals the puncture — kosher; but on the arch does not seal. Explanation: kivah shaped like arch; chelev on it outside called dakashta; inside circle called yeter — chelev in extra place on arch. Even though we rule siman 64 seif 14 chelev on yeter forbidden and tame chelev does not seal — reason here it seals because Gemara says people of Eretz Yisrael eat chelev on yeter; people of Bavel practiced forbid; nevertheless helps also Babylonians who permit through sealing puncture; but on arch forbidden to eat for everyone — therefore does not seal. Taz s.k. 1; from Gemara and Beit Yosef; see below ot 7.`,
    '2#_': `(2) Chelev on the arch — if safek arose one should be stringent for forbidden to everyone; first version is primary. Turei Beit Shmuel ot 2; She'arim ot 1; Machatzit HaShekel ot 1; Zivchei Tzedek ot 1.`,
    '3#_': `(3) And if we find a place that practiced leniency in dakashta for eating or even only for sealing — one may nullify their custom. Turei Beit Shmuel there; Machatzit HaShekel ot 3; Zivchei Tzedek ot 2; Ani Tzaddik there.`,
    '4#_': `(4) Chelev of yeter — now practiced everywhere to forbid eating; one may not be lenient for them. Beit Yosef siman 64 in name of Mahari Chaviv; Shulchan Aruch there seif 14. Machatzit HaShekel ot 4.`,
    '5#_': `(5) This specifically for Sephardim and Ashkenazim generally; but a place that practiced per Rambam's composition such as Yemen cities — or if you find a community that came from Sephardi cities and they and ancestors practiced permit yeter per Rambam and accepted so was practice in Spain — they practice their custom to permit. Machatzit HaShekel ot 5.`,
    '6#_': `(6) For majority of the world who forbid yeter — if safek arose one may permit for it is only custom and derabbanan — stringency ancestors practiced; one must practice like them. Machatzit HaShekel ot 6.`,
    '7#_': `(7) Chelev of yeter — we rule tame does not seal; there is dispute between Rashi and Rambam; per Maran Beit Yosef siman 64: for Rashi chelev outside kivah is dakashta; inside circle yeter — place of yeter meaning chelev of arch; for Rambam it is a drawn string like extra; Shach and Peri Chadash followed below siman 64 — implied from their words there is dispute; Turei Beit Shmuel concerned; wrote when such comes before rabbi must be careful sealing chelev be yeter for everyone; Maharsham ot 1 wrote therefore fallen this warning in Bira — who knows today which permitted string; and it appears in great loss all chelev from inside one may be lenient. Machatzit HaShekel ot 10; Etz Chaim there ot 3; but Taz siman 63 ot 6 wrote per our minority and knowledge we may not rely at all; worthy to forbid puncture in kivah whether from inside or outside; sealing chelev does not help at all.`,
    '8#_': `(8) [Seif 2] Kereis punctured, etc. — meaning all the kereis; also saniya dibi; also where there is no word — all mentioned are in category kereis; treifah punctured in any amount. Turei Beit Shmuel end ot 4; Machatzit HaShekel ot 3; Zivchei Tzedek ot 4.`,
    '9#_': `(9) Indeed there is a distinction: if puncture in kereis below toward ground — certainly treifah; but if puncture hidden under ribs on this side and that — safek treifah. Chochmat Adam kelal 20 ot 2; Machatzit HaShekel there; Zivchei Tzedek ot 5.`,
    '10#_': `(10) A goat stabbed between ribs near belly; secretion emerged; appeared kereis punctured; afterward lived twelve months; also impregnated and gave birth — Binat Adam ot 26; on Chochmat Adam kelal 30 to permit; wrote reason since safek dispute — twelve months and birth help as Shach siman 57 s.k. 48 — see there. However Machatzit HaShekel there rejected his words — erred; Shach Rashba and Bach did not write except in dispute of Ittur; also already disputed; we do not rely; but here dispute of amoraim in Gemara — how can one permit; see there. And so Chok L'Yisrael Yoreh De'ah part 1 siman 25 daf 34 — between dispute in Gemara and unresolved question in Gemara — twelve months pregnancy and birth do not help; but in dispute of poskim after sealing Talmud — living twelve months and birth help — see there. Beit Din Zivchei Tzedek ot 6.`,
    '11#_': `(11) There: and it has nothing to seal, etc. — part of kereis called kalyo in foreign tongue; that place is constricted; if punctured in that constricted place even if no pure chelev to seal — kosher as when punctured in attachment of meses and beit hakosot seif 7 — kosher because puncture not mafpolash outward. Sha'arei De'ah ot 4; Zivchei Tzedek ot 7.`,
    '12#_': `(12) Chelev adhering to kereis — even though people of Rhineland eat it like Rabbenu Yoel — for us who do not eat it does not seal. Beit Levi ot 4; Machatzit HaShekel ot 6; Chochmat Adam kelal 30 ot 2; Zivchei Tzedek ot 8; and implied but for Rhineland who eat it seals; and so Beit Levi there; see below siman 64 seif 9 and our words there in s.d.`,
  },
  'mateh-yehonatan': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 48 seif 2) Kereis punctured, etc. See Taz s.k. 2; they challenge why spleen should not seal like chelev on yeter — we rule like Babylonians who forbid eating chelev on yeter; nevertheless for sealing it seals as Rabbenu Nissim said "they eat" and we seal; not astonishing; if so same in kereis since Rhineland eat chelev with it — for us it should seal. They answer: granted chelev on yeter is permitted by law — halacha like R' Akiva requires attachment of membrane and peeling; chelev on yeter is not attachment but resident; Babylonians forbid from stringency — one may say "they eat," etc.; unlike chelev on kereis which we forbid — we rule like Rabbenu Efrayim; for us it is full chelev and karet liable — no language to say "they eat." Only on what Rama wrote below siman 67 seif 9: but we do not forbid vessels of Rhineland — therefore reason as Maharil in collection: that generation agreed not to forbid vessels because for essential law it appeared to rule like Rabbenu Yoel; only on chelev itself they did not wish to permit from chelev stringency; if so still difficult why not seal like chelev on yeter; and one must say: here regarding kereis since from stringency they accepted Rabbenu Efrayim's view — for us it is d'oraisa chelev with karet — therefore no "they eat"; unlike chelev on yeter which is only general stringency — we properly say "they eat," etc.`,
    '2#_': `(There seif 4) If the flesh was bored, etc., that if stretched, etc. — so Ra'ash: if bored like sela — treifah, for if stretched will stand at tefach — meaning thread surrounding the bore when stretched will be tefach; width of sela is third of tefach — end of his words. One may analyze: in bored like sela there is not a tefach length of tear — nevertheless treifah because thread surrounding bore holds tefach; if so why need deficiency of sela — even in less would be treifah if one could make one strip length tefach from the bore — for from bore one can make many strips length tefach. Rashi Orach Chaim 50b s.v. she'im timtach: if stretched here and there so width enters — length or width you find tefach in that bore — end; appears he explains width of sela is two-thirds tefach and circumference two tefachim; when stretched in length tear length tefach; if so according to his words — for us every tear without length tefach kosher; we learn nothing from thread surrounding bore — unlike Ra'ash difficulty. And that which Gemara says Rabbi Asi bored like sela treifah if stretched stands tefach; R' Chiya: for me they explained sela kosher more than like sela treifah; and mishnah taught measure in tefach — if so bored like sela treifah; must say they dispute whether sela is third tefach treifah or less than third kosher — great forcedness they dispute reality — in their times sela coins common to remove doubt. Also Shach's difficulty above siman 41 s.k. 5 calculation not precise per geometers; must say Ra'ash holds measure bored like sela treifah not because if stretched will be tefach and forbidden for tefach measure — rather treifah in itself; halacha leMoshe miSinai if bored like sela treifah even without tear length tefach. Therefore no wonder they dispute reality — all agree sela is third tefach; they dispute where halacha leMoshe miSinai applies. That which teaches "if stretched," etc. — not because treifah reason is thus; only mentions per current statement "now that bored" — halacha leMoshe miSinai; certainly if multiple punctures with much deficiency until among all like sela — also treifah like gullet and elsewhere; therefore needed to say if stretched, etc. — to teach punctures must be in one place specifically; need tefach in one place like tear — certainly here little here little do not join; same several places not one place not treifah. Therefore also Shach's difficulty resolved — bored like sela is halacha leMoshe miSinai in truth; not from tear reason; he did not care to analyze calculation; mentioned tefach though not precise; examine well.`,
    '3#_': `(There seif 7 in hagahah) And some forbid, etc. Difference between meses and beit hakosot per Tosafot for Rashi's view: beit hakosot thick — no concern lest healed; unlike meses thin — more concern. Ra'ash in sugya thorn stuck esophagus: Ra'avan ruled like Ulla; brought proof from needle in thickness beit hakosot; possible Rav Alfas distinguishes — thickness beit hakosot thick not concerned lest healed; plausible like Ra'avan — no distinction for any thickness; Tur in hints wrote Ra'ash holds like Rashi in meses puncture one side treifah; if so must distinguish thick and thin; Ra'ash certainly does not distinguish thick thin — difference meses beit hakosot: beit hakosot hard wall; meses soft wall — therefore one side also treifah. Still difficult: what proof from beit hakosot to esophagus; Taz view and Rashi implies even puncture one side through illness treifah in meses; unlike esophagus illness kosher; otherwise punctured one without other how find. From beginning Orach Chaim slight proof for Shach's view meses not forbidden one side only through thorn not illness — Gemara answers meses and beit hakosot counted as one; if so difficult for Rashi meses not equal beit hakosot in puncture — meses even one side treifah; beit hakosot must be two sides; reason there treifah one side concern lest healed; we say certainly punctured two sides and healed; if so equal beit hakosot.`,
    '4#_': `(In Shach s.k. 17) And implied in meses treifah even without korat dam outside, etc. — but from inside must be korat dam as Shach s.k. 30; ostensibly not compelled; one may say: granted beit hakosot no concern lest healed — specifically korat dam required; but in meses concern lest healed — we say there was korat dam and korat dam also returned and healed; further distinguish: granted beit hakosot korat dam required outside — for although certainly stuck from life, nevertheless without korat dam outside we say stuck from inside but not punctured outward until after death; but this we certainly do not say it stuck after death inside. If so in meses since certainly stuck from life inside — treifah even without korat dam at all — for even punctured one side treifah; but Ran and Rashba prove like Shach who challenged esophagus why thorn stuck treifah even without korat dam — why not say after slaughter punctured like beit hakosot; answered since esophagus narrow place foods liquids pass frequently — we say foods liquids passed and impossible here concern lest healed — we also say korat dam afterward healed and recovered — no difference; for in esophagus too concern lest healed; and certainly descended from life; if so korat dam neither raises nor lowers; therefore no distinction as above; also in meses korat dam required from inside.`,
    '5#_': `(There in Shulchan Aruch seif 8) If found in one needle, etc. — so Tur's language; Bach challenged: from Ra'ash proves no examination required — Ra'ash explains thorn esophagus what is written there and regarding safek derusah requires examination — see there; afterward brought Ra'avan who ruled like Ulla therefore no examination required; brings proof from needle in thickness beit hakosot; if so proves no need to turn over; answers: certainly ideally must turn over; but if salted rinsed or lost — permitted; same esophagus ideally requires examination; brings proof needle beit hakosot — see there; see siman 50 in hagahah; you will find opposite his words.`,
    '6#_': `(In Shulchan Aruch) And this is when they did not salt or rinse. See Shach s.k. 23 what he wrote in my humble opinion Rashba also concedes, etc. — this is not so; Rashba follows his view: where defect may come and no place to suspend — we do not establish on presumption; see below siman 61 what he wrote.`,
    '7#_': `(There in hagahah) And some lenient, etc., and one may rely, etc. Shach s.k. 33; here he brought Ra'ash and Rambam's words; ostensibly not precise: granted in matter stated below there is distinction expert and not expert; not so in matter lost — reason since nothing to rely on defect we establish presumption of permissibility; if so for us too even not expert; and must be that which mentions "or lost" means needle and beit hakosot lost — stated below; unknown whether punctured outward; depends on expertise — perhaps if expert puncture before us; properly required Rambam Ra'ash view no examination required — kosher even for us.`,
    '8#_': `(In Shulchan Aruch seif 11) Needle found in kurkavan, etc., suspend lenient. Because esophagus swallows; food enters through there — one may say IRC double safek inside or outside; if outside safek punctured inner organs; Shach siman 45 s.k. 5; must say because double safek examination required after korat dam; unlike reason esophagus swallows — no examination outside; those stringent forbid even in such case — not permit from double safek; one may say because found in kurkavan flesh we say because esophagus swallows we say entered through esophagus punctured esophagus exited body cavity came kurkavan outside — forced.`,
  },
  'yad-avraham': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 48 seif 4) If this flesh was bored in circle or length if more than sela — treifah if this tear stretched will stand tefach. Appears to learn: in large animal tear measure tefach; in small animal measure is majority which is less than tefach; same in boring — if stretch tear will stand at its majority less than sela — examine well. However I saw Turei Beit Shmuel not so; see Peri Megadim and Lechem. And know: per Rambam and Shulchan Aruch previous seif if majority thickness torn — like mafpolash; same regarding bored; so clear from Rashba Tur haArukh (43) — see there; examine well. Peri Megadim simply; wondered on Shach s.k. 7. However Shach followed his long book that wrote per Rambam bored means mafpolash; if not mafpolash not bored; we estimate length width circle like sela — see there. Peri Megadim challenged: Gemara says if stretched stands tefach — implies because of tefach; if so even not mafpolash; no proof — nevertheless lenient from tefach measure in small animal as Turei Beit Shmuel wrote. Thus bored in circle no majority in length or width alone lenient; for this reason lenient also not mafpolash — only helps in mafpolash since no majority on one side only in circle. And in my humble opinion bring proof for Rambam — resolves Tosafot Orach Chaim 43 s.v. henakh, etc. — majority outer torn and flesh covering also counted as one; so Turei Beit Shmuel. What wondered on Beit Yosef — Rambam holds puncture to cavity requires examination — Shach already preceded in long book.`,
    '2#_': `(Seif 8) And if the needle passed from side to side while still stuck, etc., they examine; if no korat dam found after slaughter forced through kosher if not salted; but if salted — treifah even without korat dam — lest salt removed it. In my humble opinion learned from Avodah Zarah 32b; Rashi, Rif, Ra'ash, Ran, Semak regarding Lebuvin hides — round tear opposite heart forbidden in benefit; we say in Gemara and those poskim: if korat dam on it — then certainly from life; if no korat dam — we say after slaughter torn; and there: and when not salted; but salted — say salt removed prohibition even without korat dam. Clear proof for Shulchan Aruch. Not like Hagahot Asheri chapter 1 doubtful in this law if rinsed or salted whether we say shechutah hutrah — see there. Not so — we do not say thus unless there is reason to suspend it happened after slaughter as hagahah siman 50. Do not challenge Lebuvin hides: he said if korat dam — if no korat dam we say after slaughter; Gemara Orach Chaim 51 all general punctures where nothing to draw blood like needle thorn in puncture — no korat dam required; possible from life yet no korat dam — wiped by moisture of flesh with nothing to draw; one may say blood wiped by flesh moisture as Rashi there — see there; unlike hides blood can cling in hair; since no korat dam and not salted — certainly after slaughter; and who omitted this in Hilchot Avodah Zarah chapter 7 — appears because of difficulty above and holds that sugya pushed aside Chullin sugya we rule where nothing to draw no korat dam required; settles Lechem Mishneh's wonder there.`,
    '3#_': `(Seif 11) Needle found in kurkavan all swallowed in flesh thickness not recognizable any side — suspend lenient, etc. Hagahah: some stringent; concern their words if not great loss. Appears simple: if kofa inward — toward kurkavan side; point toward cavity — kosher for in kofa cannot puncture if kofa like date pit as siman 41 seif 6; so Ra'ash Orach Chaim regarding needle found in thigh thickness; Tur Yoreh De'ah siman 91 seif 3 implies explicitly when not recognizable any side; nevertheless if kofa outward — kosher; I would have said forbid kofa toward cavity; on this he gave reason its way to scrape wall; even kofa toward cavity enters — see there; but kofa outward without that — kosher.`,
  },
  'yad-ephraim': {
    '1#_': `And it has nothing to seal it for the chelev. Be'er Heitev; see above siman 46 s.k. 3 where I wrote Beit Yosef's responsum and other responsa on this; and what he wrote regarding swollen chicken — see below siman 50; regarding worms see what I wrote in Binat Adam siman 36 and pamphlet of responsa there.`,
    '2#_': `But since most of the thickness was torn. Be'er Heitev; see in Chinuch Beit Yosef siman 40 — woman dealing with kereis to clean; while dragging secretion and passing knife saw needle crossed with secretion; see Radbaz part 2 siman 227 kereis needle stuck not visible inside; see Maharam Alashkar flesh covering majority kereis torn or bored; Shulchan Aruch responsa part 8 siman 12 round puncture between ribs — no concern derusah in round puncture as Zevachim chapter of mixtures; and all that can be suspended to illness we suspend; if cannot suspend to illness such as flesh around puncture healthy not punctured as illness way; also no concern lest punctured by thorn — thin puncture impossible to examine thin puncture — for you said puncture large; many times came before me told gored by horn and I permitted after examination; see Pri Tevuah siman 40 protrusion in animal from goring oxen.`,
    '3#_': `And so is the practice. See Be'er Heitev; Noda BiYehudah Tinyana siman 69 wrote if adhesion there and not adhesion exactly opposite stuck needle inside beit hakosot — do not forbid if needle in thick place; but in thin place since even without adhesion cannot permit except in great loss — if adhesion even if needle not stuck exactly opposite — do not be lenient even in great loss; if time of pressure also near Shabbat and Yom Tov — one may settle the matter — see there; see Mordechai seif 22 needle stuck in skin beit hakosot and from there adhered to liver courtyard.`,
    '4#_': `Needle found in cavity of body — treifah. Shulchan Aruch Yoreh De'ah part 2 siman 64 beit hakosot — needle stuck along wall; rabbi immediately declared treifah; answered if lying within skin like bolt not recognizable whence came — stringent not in great loss; but usually coarse case has great loss and may permit if needle not recognizable from side to side and korat dam outside or wart or adhered elsewhere as Kaf HaChayim kelal 89; requires further study; he is Tzitz Eliezer siman 49; nevertheless adhesion literally in eye we require; but if slightly swollen outside and no change in flesh to defect — no treifah — comes from pain of needle stuck in live flesh; do not add to treifot; but korat dam outside or adhesion and similar outside — needle found even if not stuck — declare treifah lest punctured and healed; in great loss rely on Tzitz Eliezer and Peri Chadash who are lenient also in this — see there he wrote open rebuke on rabbi who immediately declared treifah though had basis to rely; nevertheless Torah protects Israel's money; should be moderate in ruling; sages said student may not rule where his rabbi is unless three parsa away; all the more our rabbis are the books spread among Israel — whoever reaches ruling should not rule any ruling without first examining book; so I received from my teachers of blessed memory; especially I heard so from my master the famous Gaon Maharsham who sat on ruling chair in Prague community forty years; nevertheless did not rule without examining book first in Be'er Heitev; and relied on matter then not ashamed to look, etc.; and bar min dan worthy to do so where they are not Torah scholars and will not suspect them of stringency not according to law from piety and similar; he is not concerned about loss of their money — for he ruled thus without examining book, etc.; and this is not stealing people's minds but "you shall be clean," etc. — see there.`,
    '5#_': `If he is sharp. See Be'er Heitev; Noda BiYehudah Tinyana siman 30 — gentile butcher; Jewish slaughterer with him; sold innards to gentile and Jew saw removed from meses one nail that was above; unknown if in place where they pour into each other; butcher gentile whose way to mark which animal slaughtered first says sold to gentile is from first animal — forbid first and permit others; see responsum Chinuch Beit Yosef siman 91 — Israel sold kereis with innards to gentile; gentile came said found needle stuck in kereis.`,
  },
  'rabbi-akiva-eiger-yd': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 48 Shach s.k. 19) That it is at rest forever. Accordingly when needle not found stuck in it — concern lest punctured outward and healed — requires further study for practical law.`,
    '2#_': `(Seif 8 in hagahah) If it is great loss. Conclusion of acharonim: needle found stuck in beit hakosot from one side and opposite outside korat dam; likewise stuck from both sides across even without korat dam — treifah even in great loss. Found stuck one side examined no korat dam outside — kosher even not in great loss. If lost without examination or rinsed — no need to examine. Likewise needle lying in beit hakosot korat dam found outside opposite needle — kosher in great loss. In meses and in beit hakosot thin place stuck one side korat dam inside — kosher only in great loss. No korat dam at all — kosher without great loss. [And rinsed from inside impossible examine and examined outside no korat dam — requires further study.] Rust or adhesion — law like korat dam. Not called punctured one side unless examined not from side to side; but without examination even if by touch felt needle does not emerge outside — nevertheless law as punctured two sides; nevertheless in such case Bach lenient in great loss — one may rely on Bach to be lenient.`,
    '3#_': `(Taz s.k. 19) And this is with mesalleles. In Menachem Tziyon kelal 50 s.k. 7 wrote these matters contradict what Taz wrote below (siman 122 s.k. 4) end that believed even without mesalleles forbidden; and so Shach above (siman 47 s.k. 24); and so is primary.`,
  },
};
